<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  ===================================================================================================
  UI_System - "Monitor del Sistema" dashboard
  Canvas 1440 x 900. The custom window chrome owns y 0..46, so all content starts at y >= 46.

  DESIGN PX / UISCALE (Opción A)
  ==============================
    Authors work in design pixels (1440x900). UI_LAYOUT holds designWidth/Height + uiScale
    (default 1.0). Opt-in: this layout has a <stylesheet>, so IsUIScaleActive() is true.
    Layouts without stylesheet (e.g. UI_Options) ignore UIScale and stay XML-only.
    scale=1.0 must remain visually identical to the Fase 0 baseline.

  COORDINATE CONVENTION
  =====================
    ROOT element   : ypos = BOTTOM edge, measured downwards from the top of the screen.
                     A card whose top must sit at y=70 with height 390  ->  ypos = 460.
    CHILD element  : ypos = distance UPWARDS from the FATHER's bottom edge.
                     xpos = distance rightwards from the FATHER's left edge.
    Tokens accepted: xpos = left|right|center , ypos = up|down|center , width/height = max|auto.

  CONTRACT WITH UI_System.cpp  (do not rename these without updating the source)
  =============================================================================
    cpu_temp_bar            progressimage      SetLevel()
    cpu_usage_radial        progressradial     SetLevel()
    cpu_history_chart       statisticschart    HistoryChart_Apply()  CPU / Memoria / Disco
    card_datetime           form               default in same slot (always unless chart)
    ram_usage_radial        progressradial     SetLevel()
    ram_linear_bar          progressbar     SetLevel()
    disk_usage_radial       progressradial  SetLevel()
    disk_linear_bar         progressbar     SetLevel()
    disk_prev_btn/next_btn  button          cycle volumes (HardwareInfo_CycleDisk)
    connection_icon_ok/ko   image           SetVisible()   (green tick / red cross)
    nav-<section>-btn       button          click target + SetSelected()
    nav-<section>-row       form            SetSelected() so CSS `form.nav-row:selected .nav-label` works
    #[MASK] literals        resolved in UI_SYSTEM::UserInterface_ChangeLiteralText()

  Selection chrome is stylesheet-only (:selected on button + row). Legacy nav-*-hl / nav-*-bar overlays
  were removed; do not reintroduce SetVisible band hacks in the app.

  MARGIN AUTHORING (stylesheet present)
  =====================================
    4-value margin is CSS TRBL: TOP, RIGHT, BOTTOM, LEFT.
    Longhands margin-top / margin-right / margin-bottom / margin-left override the shorthand.
    (Layouts WITHOUT a stylesheet keep LEFT,RIGHT,UP,DOWN and ignore margin-* -- UI_Options.)

  WHAT LIVES WHERE
  ================
    Only the BASE properties reach the stylesheet (UI_MANAGER::GetLayoutElement_Base is the single
    builder that reads the cascaded UI_STYLE bag). Type-specific attributes == sizefont, level,
    thickness, gradientcolor, gradientmode, linecolor, roundcap, startangle, sweepangle,
    allocationtext, progressrect, imageempty/imagefull, offsetstart/offsetend == are read straight
    from this XML by the per-type builders and are INVISIBLE to dashboard.css. Colours, radii,
    padding, borders and shadows live in the stylesheet.
  ===================================================================================================
-->
<layouts>

  <skin name="" drawmode="canvas" rasterfont="verdana18" vectorfont="Nunito-SemiBold.ttf" backgroundcolor="13,17,23"></skin>

  <stylesheet>dashboard.css</stylesheet>

  <layout name="dashboard" backgroundcolor="13,17,23" designwidth="1440" designheight="900">

    <!-- ==========================================================================================
         SURFACES  (drawn first, everything else sits on top)
         ========================================================================================== -->

