    <!-- Phase 4 ("migración del ejemplo", second sub-step): the FIRST real nested flex container in this file
         ; see dashboard.css's ".footer" rule (display: flex) and its own SCOPE comment. The eight children
         below are real XML children now (were root-level siblings, hand-positioned in absolute canvas
         coordinates); they are listed in actual LEFT-TO-RIGHT VISUAL order (flex packs in document/compose
         order along the main axis ; this engine has no reordering property), which is NOT the order the old
         flat version of this file listed them in (dividers first, then each icon/text pair). No xpos/ypos on
         any child: position now comes entirely from the flex engine (row direction, flex-start justify-
         content/align-items ; all just the engine's own defaults, left unset here) plus each child's own
         "margin" ; see each one's inline "style=" below for exactly how the four numbers reproduce this
         element's ORIGINAL absolute position pixel-for-pixel:
           - horizontal (main axis): margin-LEFT is the gap from the PRECEDING child's right edge (or, for the
             first child, from the container's own left edge) ; derived as
             (this child's old absolute xpos) - (preceding child's old absolute xpos + its width).
           - vertical (cross axis): NONE of the eight children set a vertical margin or "align-self" any more
             (an earlier version of this comment walked through per-item margin-UP/margin-DOWN arithmetic
             here ; superseded by this simpler, more robust approach after two rounds of live-app regressions:
             (1) shipping margin-UP on the assumption a text element's box has height 0 ; wrong, see
             UI_SKINCANVAS::CalculateBoundaryLine_Text(), it auto-sizes to the real font-metric height, which
             clipped the captions off-screen; (2) the align-self:flex-end + margin-DOWN fix that followed was
             correct in isolation but put the three captions on a different cross-axis baseline than their own
             icons (still margin-UP-centered), which ; once the captions were finally visible ; visually read
             as "not vertically centered" and, combined with a too-tight 8px gap, "glued together". Both are
             fixed at once by centering the WHOLE row instead of each item individually: dashboard.css's
             ".footer" rule now carries "align-items: center;" (the engine's own PackFlexLine() cross-axis
             centering, height-independent by construction ; see UI_LAYOUTENGINE.cpp), so every child ;
             image, form, or text, whatever its real auto-measured height turns out to be ; lands vertically
             centered in the footer's 44px automatically, with NO per-item vertical arithmetic to keep in sync.
           - horizontal (main axis): unchanged from the earlier derivation EXCEPT the icon-to-caption gap, which
             is now 12 (was 8, still each caption's own margin-LEFT) ; purely a visual tweak: the tighter 8
             read as the icon and its caption "touching" once both sat on the same (now centered) baseline.
             Every OTHER margin-LEFT (divider-after-caption, next icon-after-divider: 232/219/216) is still the
             gap from the PRECEDING child's right edge, derived from the ORIGINAL absolute mockup exactly as
             before ; see the earlier revision of this comment for the full derivation. Note those numbers
             only reproduce the mockup's pixel positions as long as each caption's real auto-measured string
             width roughly matches what the mockup assumed; because a caption's width is its own real,
             font-measured string width (not a fixed placeholder) ; e.g. "SO: <the live OS string>" ; the
             exact position of everything after the FIRST caption is inherently dynamic now, unlike the single
             fixed-size mockup this file replaced, which could not do that at all.

         SCOPE ADDENDUM (footer icon/caption gap regression, round 3 ; root cause confirmed against a real
         windowed build, not just this suite's unit tests): every child below now also carries "flex-shrink: 0"
         in its inline style. Without it, each child fell back to the engine's CSS default (flex-shrink: 1), and
         UI_MANAGER::ChangeTextElementValue()'s live-reflow fix (round 1 ; re-running RunLayout() on every
         "#[FOOTER_*]" text refresh so siblings stay correctly spaced, per THIS SAME comment's own history above)
         re-engaged that shrink on every single refresh. Live "SO: <full OS string>" and "Uptime: ..." captions
         genuinely run wider than this row's fixed 232/219/216 gap margins were sized for (see the paragraph
         above), so the row is a few percent over budget the moment those two captions are both long ; and each
         RunLayout() call was shrinking every child a little further using the PREVIOUS call's already-shrunk
         width as its new "natural" size (fixed engine-side in UI_LAYOUTENGINE::BuildTree()/UI_SKIN::
         CalculateBoundaryLine() ; see their own SCOPE ADDENDUM comments), geometrically converging the 36px
         icons down to a third of their size after a couple of minutes on screen and, with it, their caption's
         margin-left-computed gap. "flex-shrink: 0" restores this row's actual intent ; every icon, divider and
         caption stays EXACTLY its declared/measured size, full stop ; so on the (accepted, pre-existing, see
         above) days the live captions run long, the row simply overflows a little past x=1440 instead of
         quietly shrinking every icon and gap to disguise it. -->
    <element name="footer_bg" type="form" class="footer" xpos="0" ypos="900" width="1440" height="44">
      <element name="footer_equipo_icon" type="image" style="margin: 0,0,0,24; flex-shrink: 0;"   width="36" height="36">icons/foot_computer.svg</element>
      <element name="footer_equipo_text" type="text"  class="foot" style="margin: 0,0,0,16; flex-shrink: 0;">#[FOOTER_EQUIPO]</element>
      <element name="footer_so_icon"     type="image" style="margin: 0,0,0,28; flex-shrink: 0;"  width="36" height="36">icons/foot_gear.svg</element>
      <element name="footer_so_text"     type="text"  class="foot" style="margin: 0,0,0,16; flex-shrink: 0;">#[FOOTER_SO]</element>
      <element name="footer_divider_2"   type="form"  class="hr-line" style="margin: 0,0,0,28; flex-shrink: 0;" width="1" height="24"></element>
      <!-- Invisible spacer pushes Uptime flush right; padding-left:210 on form.footer keeps Equipo clear of the sidebar. -->
      <element name="footer_spacer"      type="form"  style="flex-grow: 1; background-color: 0,0,0,0; border-width: 0;" width="0" height="0"></element>
      <element name="footer_uptime_icon" type="image" style="margin: 0,0,0,0; flex-shrink: 0;"  width="36" height="36">icons/foot_clock.svg</element>
      <element name="footer_uptime_text" type="text"  class="foot" style="margin: 0,24,0,16; flex-shrink: 0;">#[FOOTER_UPTIME]</element>
    </element>

    <!-- Cards
         Phase 4 ("migración del ejemplo", fourth sub-step): each card's header (icon + title) is now a real
         XML child ("card-header") instead of two root-level siblings ("<name>_hdr_icon"/"<name>_hdr_text")
         hand-positioned in absolute canvas coordinates ; see dashboard.css's "form.card"/"form.card-header"
         rules for the flex/padding properties this relies on. Approved SCOPE for this round is header-only:
         each card's BODY content (progress widgets, values, captions ; everything below the "CARD N" banner
         comments further down this file) stays exactly as it was, flat root-level siblings, untouched.

         Z-ORDER: unlike the sidebar's icon/label (which shared their screen region with a later-declared
         "nav-<section>-hl"/"-bar" overlay, forcing a separate wrapper ; see "sidebar_nav"'s own comment),
         no card header shares its screen region with any element declared between "card_cpu_temp" (here)
         and where the old "<name>_hdr_icon"/"<name>_hdr_text" used to sit (datetime_box/uptime_box/dividers,
         the sidebar, the brand block ; all elsewhere on screen). So nesting straight into "card_<name>"
         itself, no wrapper trick needed, reproduces the original paint order with no visible difference.

         DERIVATION (traced back to the ORIGINAL absolute positions this replaces, identical relative geometry
         confirmed across all 6 cards): each header icon sat at a card-relative offset of (24, 12) ; e.g. card
         1: card xpos=238, "temp_hdr_icon" xpos=262 (238+24); reproduced below as "card-header"'s own margin,
         "margin: 12,0,0,24;" (TOP=12, LEFT=24 -- CSS TRBL), the same division of responsibility already used for "footer"/
         "sidebar-nav" (father padding 0, child margin does the positioning ; see "form.card"'s own comment).
         Within the row, the title text's old xpos was always exactly 82 from the card's left edge, i.e. a 10px
         gap from the icon's right edge (82 - (24+48) = 10) ; reproduced as the title's own "margin: 0,0,0,10;"
         (LEFT=10, first flex item being the icon with no leading margin of its own). Vertically, "align-items:
         center" on "card-header" (row height = the icon's own 48, "form.card-header" in dashboard.css) replaces
         each title's individually hand-picked ypos, using the SAME real-height-independent centering already
         proven for "footer"/"nav-row" rather than re-deriving one more hand-pinned offset per card. -->
    <!-- Track L.1: top row of three cards in CSS grid (same 238/460 origin; 376 cols + 22 gap). -->
    <element name="cards_grid" type="form" class="cards-grid" xpos="238" ypos="460" width="1172" height="390">
    <element name="card_cpu_temp"   type="form" class="card" width="376" height="390">
      <!-- Longhands demo (Phase C): same inset as margin: 12,0,0,24 -- easier to read than TRBL shorthand. -->
      <element name="card-header" type="form" class="card-header" style="margin-top: 12; margin-left: 24;" width="328" height="48">
        <element name="temp_hdr_icon" type="image" width="48" height="48">icons/card_thermo.svg</element>
        <element name="temp_hdr_text" type="text" class="card-title card-title-lg" style="margin-left: 10;">Temperatura CPU</element>
      </element>
      <!-- "temp_hdr_icon"/"temp_hdr_text" (icon at card-relative 24,12; title 82 from the card's left edge,
           a 10px gap from the icon) moved into "card_cpu_temp" itself as a nested "card-header" ; see this
           file's own comment on the "Cards" section above and dashboard.css's "form.card-header". The
           xpos=262/466 reasoning in the comment just below still holds unchanged: "temp_hdr_icon" still sits
           at that same absolute x, now arrived at via the card's xpos (238) + the header's margin (24)
           instead of a hand-typed xpos. -->

      <!-- thermo_empty.png/thermo_full.png are the "glass tube" artwork supplied by the designer, with the
           0/20/40/60/80/100 numeric scale and the "°C" unit baked directly into the bitmap (unlike the earlier
           flat icons, which needed separate temp_scale_* text elements to show a scale at all, now removed).
           Draw_ProgressImage draws these at their native pixel size (PutBitmapAlpha), so the on-screen size comes
           from the PNG's own dimensions (180x270, scaled up from the mockup comparison) rather than from
           width/height here; those two attributes are kept in sync with the asset purely for layout/hit-region
           bookkeeping. There is still no CSS color/tint hook for this widget type, so the tube's color stays
           whatever the bitmap contains.
           offsetstart/offsetend were measured directly against the 180x270 asset, not guessed proportionally:
           the tube's own red fill (in thermo_full.png) starts at pixel row 25, right where the rounded top cap
           reaches its full width, and the bulb's fixed red disc (identical in both images, so it does not need
           "revealing" at all) begins at row 193; hence offsetend=25 (top margin) and offsetstart=270-193=77
           (bottom margin).

           Column layout (xpos=262/466 below): the card's own left inner margin is 24 (card left=238, and
           temp_hdr_icon already sits at x=262 above), so the tube's left edge was moved to xpos=262 to reuse
           that exact same margin and to line up under the header icon. The right-hand group (cpu_temp_value,
           temp_cap_icon, temp_cap_text) is placed at xpos=466, i.e. the same 24-unit gap again measured from the
           tube's own right edge (262+180+24=466), so the left margin of the tube and the gap between the tube
           and the right-hand group are equal, as requested. All three right-hand elements share that same
           xpos=466 so they line up vertically with each other; 466+142=608 stays inside the card's right edge
           (614) even for the widest live value, "100°C" at sizefont 50 (measured against Nunito-SemiBold.ttf).

           Vertical position (ypos below) was re-measured against Abraham's clean reference crop of the target
           card: mapping that reference's own card rectangle onto this card's coordinates (both are ~376x390),
           the tube's bottom edge sits at ~87% of the card's height and the value/icon/caption group sits noticeably
           higher/tighter than our previous ypos values, so all four were raised: cpu_temp_bar ypos 416->405 (kept
           clear of temp_hdr_icon, whose bottom edge is at y=130, by 5 units), cpu_temp_value 276->263, temp_cap_icon
           377->364, temp_cap_text 402->389; a uniform ~13-unit rise that preserves the spacing already measured
           between them (it matched the reference closely) while moving the whole block up to match. The reference's
           tube is proportionally narrower than this 180-wide asset (drawn at native pixel size, so width/height
           above cannot itself compensate); xpos=262/466 already matches the reference's horizontal fractions
           closely (measured within ~1%), so only the vertical position needed correcting here. -->
      <!-- Phase 4 ("migración del ejemplo", fifth sub-step: "card bodies"): nested into "card_cpu_temp" as a real
           XML child instead of 5 root-level siblings hand-positioned in absolute canvas coordinates. Structure:
           "card-body" (flex row) = [cpu_temp_bar] + [right-col (flex column) = [value-row (flex row) =
           cpu_temp_value+cpu_temp_unit] + temp_cap_icon + temp_cap_text]. "card-body"'s own margin (24,0,5,0)
           reproduces the original absolute geometry: LEFT=24 lines the thermometer's left edge up with the
           header icon's (both 24 in from the card's own left edge, see "card-header"'s own derivation comment);
           UP=5 is the original 5px clearance kept between the header's bottom (12+48=60 from the card top) and
           the thermometer's own original top edge. "column-gap: 24" between the two children reproduces the
           original 24px gap from the thermometer's right edge (262+180=442) to the right-column's original left
           edge (466). Vertical spacing INSIDE the right column (temp_cap_icon's/temp_cap_text's own margin-top
           below) could not be re-derived by the same exact arithmetic the header used: unlike an image/icon, a
           "text" element's real rendered height is a runtime, font-metrics-dependent measurement GEN does not
           expose statically to this XML, so those two numbers are reasonable STARTING estimates, tuned against
           Abraham's real Windows build the same iterative way nearly every other pixel value in this file
           already was (see e.g. "temp_cap_text"'s own old 4px xpos note, kept below), not values with the same
           load-bearing precision as "card-header"'s derivation. -->
      <!-- "card-body"/"right-col"/"value-row" all carry an explicit width AND height: CalculateBoundaryLine_Form()
           always returns false (a plain "form" never auto-sizes to its children, unlike text/image/progress*
           widgets, which measure themselves from font metrics/asset dimensions/explicit attributes) ; an
           un-sized flex wrapper reads as a 0x0 box to UI_LAYOUTENGINE, and a 0-sized MAIN axis makes
           ResolveFlexItemSizes() compute a large NEGATIVE freespace against that wrapper's own real children,
           wrongly shrinking them (every item defaults to flex-shrink:1). Each size below is a generous, safely
           non-shrinking bound (not a load-bearing pixel-exact value): 346 = 180 (thermometer) + 24 (gap) + 142
           (right column, matching the original design's own "466+142=608 stays inside the card's right edge"
           bound); 270 matches the thermometer's own height, the tallest of "card-body"'s two children; 247 =
           62 (value-row, sized to the largest live value's real sizefont=50 glyph height) + 100 (gap to the
           caption icon) + 60 (icon) + 7 (gap) + ~18 (caption text's real height). -->
      <!-- right-col centrado interno; el aire L/R de la tarjeta lo define form.temp-card-body
           (margin 24 + width 328). No encojer right-col por debajo de 142. -->
      <element name="card-body" type="form" class="flex-row temp-card-body" width="328" height="270">
        <element name="cpu_temp_bar" type="progressimage" width="180" height="270"
                 direction="vertical" allocationtext="none"
                 offsetstart="77" offsetend="25" level="0"
                 imageempty="thermo_empty.png" imagefull="thermo_full.png">
        </element>

        <element name="right-col" type="form" class="flex-col temp-right-col" style="justify-content: center; align-items: center;" width="142" height="220">
          <element name="value-row" type="form" class="flex-row" style="align-items: flex-end; justify-content: center;" width="142" height="62">
            <element name="cpu_temp_value" type="text" class="value-temp" sizefont="50">#[CPU_TEMPERATURE]</element>
            <element name="cpu_temp_unit" type="text" class="value-temp" style="margin: 0,0,0,6;" sizefont="28">°C</element>
          </element>

          <element name="temp_cap_icon" type="image" style="margin: 20,0,0,0;" width="52" height="52">icons/cap_cpu.svg</element>
          <element name="temp_cap_text" type="text" class="label" style="margin: 8,0,0,0; text-align: center;" sizefont="14">Temperatura actual</element>
        </element>
      </element>
    </element>
    <element name="card_cpu_usage"  type="form" class="card" width="376" height="390">
      <element name="card-header" type="form" class="card-header" style="margin: 12,0,0,24;" width="328" height="48">
        <element name="cpu_hdr_icon" type="image" width="48" height="48">icons/card_cpu.svg</element>
        <element name="cpu_hdr_text" type="text" class="card-title card-title-lg" style="margin: 0,0,0,10;">Uso actual de CPU</element>
      </element>
      <!-- Restored Phase-pre-0 radial card (kept for production CPU usage). Chart moved to card_cpu_history. -->
      <element name="card-body" type="form" class="flex-col cpu-usage-body" width="232" height="310">
        <element name="cpu_usage_radial" type="progressradial" class="ring-cpu"
                 width="220" height="220"
                 level="0" thickness="18" roundcap="yes" startangle="-90" sweepangle="360"
                 gradientcolor="56,139,253" gradientmode="track">
          <element name="cpu_usage_value" type="text" class="ring-value" xpos="center" ypos="center" sizefont="54" maxsizetext="4">#[PROGRESSBAR_PERCENT]</element>
        </element>

        <element name="cpu-usage-caption-slot" type="form" class="flex-row cpu-usage-caption" style="align-items: center; justify-content: center;" width="232" height="24">
          <element name="cpu_usage_caption" type="text" class="label-accent" sizefont="16">Uso actual</element>
        </element>
      </element>
    </element>
    <element name="card_ram"        type="form" class="card" width="376" height="390">
      <element name="card-header" type="form" class="card-header" style="margin: 12,0,0,24;" width="328" height="48">
        <element name="ram_hdr_icon" type="image" width="48" height="48">icons/card_ram.svg</element>
        <element name="ram_hdr_text" type="text" class="card-title" style="margin: 0,0,0,10;">Consumo de memoria RAM</element>
      </element>
      <!-- Phase 4 ("migración del ejemplo", fifth sub-step: "card bodies"): nested into "card_ram" as a real XML
           child. Structure: "card-body" (flex row) = [ram_usage_radial] + [right-col (flex column) =
           ram_used_total + ram_caption + ram_linear_bar + scale-row (flex row, justify-content: space-between) =
           ram_scale_0/50/100]. "card-body"'s own margin (22,0,58,0) reproduces the ring's original left/top edge
           (LEFT=22, matching the ring's original 1056-1034 offset from the card's own left edge; UP=58, the
           ring's original top edge 188 minus the header row's bottom edge 130). "right-col"'s own margin-top
           (38) reproduces the vertical gap between the ring's top and the used/total text's original top ; this
           column starts noticeably lower than the ring, matching the mockup. Every OTHER vertical gap inside
           "right-col" (ram_caption/ram_linear_bar/scale-row's own margin-top below), like "card_cpu_temp"'s own
           caveat, is a reasonable STARTING estimate rather than an exact derivation: a "text" element's real
           rendered height is a runtime, font-metrics-dependent measurement this XML cannot see statically, so
           these were tuned against Abraham's real Windows build, the same iterative process nearly every other
           pixel value in this file already went through. "ram_linear_bar"/"scale-row" both carry an extra 6px
           margin-left, matching the original design's own ~6px rightward shift of the bar/scale row relative to
           "ram_used_total"'s column (1256 vs 1250). "scale-row" is given the SAME width as the bar (140) so
           "justify-content: space-between" spreads "0%"/"50%"/"100%" across it exactly like their original
           1256/1313/1363 xpos ladder did by hand. -->
      <!-- Explicit width/height, same reason as "card_cpu_temp"'s own "card-body" comment: an un-sized "form"
           flex wrapper reads as 0x0 to UI_LAYOUTENGINE and wrongly shrinks its real children.
           354 = 178 (ring) + 16 (gap) + 160 (right column ; see its own comment below for that number's
           derivation); 186 is generous headroom for "right-col"'s real content, which (including its own
           38px margin-top) runs taller than the ring alone. -->
      <!-- RAM: anillo sin glow, mas pequeño para dejar margen con la columna de textos/barra. -->
      <element name="card-body" type="form" class="flex-row" style="margin: 36,0,0,24; column-gap: 22; align-items: center;" width="328" height="200">
        <element name="ram_usage_radial" type="progressradial" class="ring-ram"
                 width="140" height="140"
                 level="0" thickness="16" roundcap="yes" startangle="-90" sweepangle="360"
                 gradientcolor="163,113,247" gradientmode="track">
          <element name="ram_usage_value" type="text" class="ring-value" xpos="center" ypos="center" sizefont="32" maxsizetext="4">#[PROGRESSBAR_PERCENT]</element>
        </element>

        <element name="right-col" type="form" class="flex-col" style="justify-content: center;" width="166" height="160">
          <element name="ram-used-row" type="form" class="flex-row" style="align-items: flex-end;" width="166" height="28">
            <element name="ram_used"  type="text" class="value-ram" sizefont="22">#[RAM_USED]</element>
            <element name="ram_total" type="text" class="label-dim" style="margin: 0,0,0,4;" sizefont="16">#[RAM_TOTAL]</element>
          </element>
          <element name="ram_caption"    type="text" class="label"     style="margin: 8,0,0,0;" sizefont="13">En uso / Total</element>

          <element name="ram_linear_bar" type="progressbar" class="bar-ram" width="160" height="14"
                   style="margin: 28,0,0,0;" allocationtext="none" direction="horizontal"
                   roundcap="yes" progressrect="0,0,160,14" level="0" linecolor="0,0,0,0"
                   gradientcolor="163,113,247" gradientmode="track">
          </element>

          <!-- Scale = same 160px as bar. Three fixed slots + text-align (not space-between on glyph widths). -->
          <element name="scale-row" type="form" class="flex-row" style="margin: 8,0,0,0;" width="160" height="15">
            <element name="ram_scale_0"   type="text" class="label-dim" width="53" height="15" style="text-align: left;   flex-shrink: 0; flex-grow: 0;" sizefont="11">0%</element>
            <element name="ram_scale_50"  type="text" class="label-dim" width="54" height="15" style="text-align: center; flex-shrink: 0; flex-grow: 0;" sizefont="11">50%</element>
            <element name="ram_scale_100" type="text" class="label-dim" width="53" height="15" style="text-align: right;  flex-shrink: 0; flex-grow: 0;" sizefont="11">100%</element>
          </element>
        </element>
      </element>
    </element>
